<description>
Simulate tokens falling through a pipe network after gates rotate open.

Input structure:
- Wall (0), bg (pipe fill), gate (horizontal 1×3 bars), token (small edge pixels).

Rule:
- Rotate each gate into a vertical blocker; gate cells become bg.
- Tokens drop downward through bg, choosing the extreme column for their side (left→min, right→max).
- Tokens settle at true pipe ends (adjacent to wall/boundary), packing inward.

Key insight: Tokens select drop columns by entry side and land at wall-bounded endpoints, ignoring blocker-bounded ones.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "3x3 square with orange horizontal bar in middel row",
  "transform": "rot90, orange bar change to magenta",
  "type2": "move_along_path",
  "src2": "green pixel",
  "path2": "along teal pixels",
  "trajectory2": "invisible",
  "dst2": "endpoint of path next to grid edge",
  "multi_step": "rotate_in_place then move_along_path"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 11-19 rows (odd) x 16-19 cols; H = 2*N+1 where N = 5-9 wall rows
  colors: wall=0, token=3, open_post=6(output only), gate=7, bg=8
  layout: |
    Alternating rows: even=pipe(bg=8), odd=wall(all 0 except gates).
    Last row (even) is pipe with no edge tokens. All other pipe rows
    have token=3 at col 0 and col W-1 (2 tokens per non-last pipe row).
  gates:
    shape: 1x3 horizontal bar of color 7 in wall rows
    count_per_wall: 0-3
    total: 6-12 across all wall rows
    center_col: 2 to W-3 (flanks stay interior to grid)
    min_spacing: 5 between adjacent gate centers in same wall row [observed]
    cross_wall_gap: gate centers from adjacent wall rows must differ by >= 2 columns
  holes:
    desc: single-cell 0 in pipe rows (not at col 0 or W-1), splits pipe into segments
    count_per_pipe_row: 0-2
    total: 0-4 across all pipe rows [observed]
  single_exit_constraint: |
    After gate opening (each gate -> 3-tall vertical 6-post at center, flanks become bg),
    every pipe segment (contiguous bg between 6-posts/holes/edges) must have
    <=1 exit below and <=1 entry above. For 2 gates in same wall row with
    centers c1<c2 and c2-c1>2: a separator (6-post from adjacent wall's gate
    or hole) must exist between c1+1 and c2-1 in both pipe rows above and below.
  transformation: |
    1. Rotate each gate: 3 cells->bg, center col gets vertical 6-post (rows r-1,r,r+1).
    2. Remove tokens, simulate falling: each token drops through single-exit
       segments until stuck (no exit). Drops span 0-6 levels; max per example >=3.
    3. Pack tokens at opposite end of segment from entry point. Tokens from same
       side stack inward (1-2 tokens per destination segment)./

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Pick H=2*N+1 (N in 5-9) and W in 14-20.
    - Build the opened-gate pipe network (the output state) top-down. For each
      wall row, place 0-3 gate-post columns (vertical 6-posts). Ensure the
      single-exit constraint is satisfied by construction -- when placing a new
      gate-post, verify each resulting segment in pipe rows above and below has
      <=1 exit/entry, adding holes if needed.
    - Simulate token settling in the output network to place output tokens.
      Each pipe row (except last) contributes 2 tokens (left+right edge); route
      them downward and pack at segment endpoints. Ensure at least one token
      traverses >=3 levels for non-trivial paths.
    - Invert to get input -- undo gate rotation (replace each 3-tall 6-post
      with 1x3 horizontal 7-bar in the wall row, remove 6-posts from pipe rows),
      move tokens back to edge positions (col 0 and col W-1 of their starting
      pipe rows). Holes (0 in pipe rows) remain unchanged.
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

